# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Custom Snort 3 IDS Rules
# Created for Lab 5 - Cybersecurity Network Monitoring
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Rule 1: ICMP Ping Detection
# Intent: Detects ICMP echo requests used during network reconnaissance and host discovery.
alert icmp any any -> $HOME_NET any (msg:"ICMP Ping Detected"; sid:1000001; rev:1;)

# Rule 2: SSH Connection Attempt (Port 22)
# Intent: Monitors for new TCP SYN requests to port 22 to detect unauthorized remote access attempts or brute-forcing.
alert tcp any any -> $HOME_NET 22 (msg:"SSH Connection Attempt"; flags:S; sid:1000002; rev:1;)

# Rule 3: Unencrypted FTP Traffic (Port 21)
# Intent: Monitors for insecure cleartext FTP usage, which is vulnerable to packet sniffing and data exfiltration.
alert tcp any any -> $HOME_NET 21 (msg:"Unencrypted FTP Traffic Detected"; sid:1000003; rev:1;)
